{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/475321-places-that-aren-t-the-forge-city","id":475321,"title":"Places-That-Aren't: The Forge-City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-09T20:55:51-07:00","id":475321,"title":"Places-That-Aren't: The Forge-City","content":"Another jewel of mine that I recently rediscovered, I hope you like it!<br /> ________________________<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Forge-City </b></span><br /> <br /> There are many Places-That-Aren't, some little more than closets that don't exist in the real world, or are small spaces that are a bit larger on the inside than out. Others are quite large, one being an entire floor that's not there, or even entire realms of their own within the Shadow itself. The Forge City is one such realm, one of fire and smoke and steel. Connected to the administrative office of an abandoned automotive factory in the Shadow, opening the door to the office leads to a vast and incredible realm that defies mortal logic. The Forge City is a massive collection of foundries filled with white hot materials processing tirelessly, smokestacks billowing black smoke into the midnight black sky, pits of molten Essence dotting the landscape, factories filled with machinery endlessly operating nonstop, labyrinthine streets of basalt snake in between buildings, broken only by Essence Pits or vents that which erupt into pillars of burning energy. As stated before, this realm is vast, extending for miles around in all directions, though the very city limits seem to be a circular rock wall that extends vertically in the air eternally. Another feature of this realm is that the only light to be seen comes from the city itself and it's assorted structures, as the there is no day/night cycle in this realm, only the smoke filled obsidian sky.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, this Place-That-Isn't is quite antagonistic to newcomers that haven't quite adjusted to such a harsh environment. For Uratha it quickly comes apparent just how inhospitable this place is, the air is burning hot and choked with smoke, making breathing a challenge at best and seems to burn the very essence in their bodies, inflicting a point of lethal damage every hour as well as the loss of a point of Essence. Fortunately Essence is immensely plentiful in the Forge City, the trick is to be willing to endure high levels of pain in order to harvest it. Essentially the entire realm is one giant locus, it's bounty in the form of it's rivers of molten slag and geysers of intense energy, one merely needs to reach out and reap the rewards... at the cost of their flesh that is. for every lethal damage sustained from these sources the werewolf ( or non native spirit) gains one essence. Once the werewolf has remained in the City for 24 hours they will have adapted to the realm and find that the air becomes much more breathable and the temperature, while uncomfortable, is more bearable and no longer scorches the werewolf. They still take damage from harvesting Essence from the vents and pools, but they gain 2 Essence per point of lethal, same with non native spirits who have adapted.<br /> <br /> While the Forge City itself is ripe with an abundance of Essence, the Shadow locale it is connected to is not. the Abandoned factory is essentially a Barrens from so many years of inactivity, the flow of Essence long having dried up and dissipated. How the Forge City has managed to thrive is both as interesting as it is simple. during the late 20's all the way through the 60's that particular factory had gained quite a bit of fame as it manufactured everything from automobile parts to weapons and ammunition to fighter jet components to even lesser items such as baby bottles and children toys. For so many decades the factory had become one of the symbols of what the American people could engineer, and the emotional and conceptual energies tied to the factory bloomed, forming a locus tied to the resonance of industry and production inside the head executive's office within the administrative wing of the building, a locus that rapidly gained strength and grew to a font of Essence of legendary proportions.<br /> <br /> During the early days life was good for the spirits of the factory, and Essence was immensely plentiful, with more than enough to go around. Even without the pesky Uratha to police it, the factory was quite harmonious and there were few disruptions, the spirit of the factory itself made sure of that. Christening itself the Foreman the Factory-spirit, now a powerful Incarnae of Industry, oversaw that it's fellow spirits performed their natural tasks quickly and efficiently, for doing well within the Shadow ensured rich new Essence to flow from the world of Light to feed them all even more. During this time the Foreman also worked to create a place ideal for spirits such as itself and it's brood, a space where they could dwell and never worry about the meddlesome Uratha who would surely one day come calling, or the avarious spirits of greed and exploitation that began worming their way into it's Court. By the mid 60's it finally finished it's grand task of creating it's own realm within the Shadow, transforming the office containing the locus into it's own self sustained, self sufficient space, a realm of metal and fire and industrial fantasy.<br /> <br /> This event couldn't of happened a moment too soon as not long after the factory's shadow began to weaken. What had happened as that over the years the factory's importance began to lessen and the demand for it's products became less and less as other, more attractive forms of business began appearing. The Foreman saw this and desperately tried to aid the factory by creating more products with it's Influence, and for a time this did indeed help give the factory a great edge over it's competition, but in doing so it caught the attentions of a local pack of Iron Masters and for the first time in over four decades the denizens of the factory had to defend themselves against the accursed children of Father Wolf. While the spirits and the Foreman fought fiercely, the Uratha were no careless spirits starving for Essence, and they were able to push the spirits to the brink of eradication within a few short days. Terrified of what was happening and enraged at the Uratha who dared to interfere with it's agenda, the Foreman quickly saw no other choice for survival and ushered the surviving members of it's Court into the infant Place-That-Wasn't. After the last spirit fled inside, the Incarnae too retreated within and sealed the entrance behind it, placing itself and it's court out of the werewolve's reach.<br /> <br /> Since then the factory has long fallen into disrepair. As the Foreman couldn't aid it's dying factory with it's Influence it quickly went bankrupt and was then shut down. Soon after the Shadow of and around the factory whither and slowly began to die, becoming a moderately large Barren. As for the Forge City itself it has been thriving vastly since it's isolation, becoming a sort of spiritual Galapagos as it's spirits have evolved largely without human influence (save for a few rare occasions) , and in fact actually has been growing as it's pocket space seems to be expanding. the reason for this continued prosperity is due to the City partially being kept alive due to the occasional influx of new spirits that are drawn to the factory when the door to the Forge City is opened, acting as a Siren's call. These new spirits help refresh the pools of Essence within the the City and helps inform it's &quot;citizens&quot; of the changes that have happened in the outside world, and eventually these newcomers are added to the fold and gamut of the Forge City's population, furthering the growth of this strange &quot;paradise&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-09-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:22:09-07:00","id":475416,"title":"","content":"I always like places-that-aren't. I am going to have to talk to my gm (in a multi splat game) about how I want to search for one and find a way to put it under my control. Being that the character will be a demon I can almost see this seeming to be paradise or remind them of their past life so I may steal it to show my gm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:09:26-07:00","id":476186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/475321-places-that-aren-t-the-forge-city?p=475416#post475416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div cl